      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5,100 mg/day**. That is about twice the maximum labeled daily dose. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in the US. A dose that high greatly raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO BID with meals\n- **Another dose**, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg BID\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and add a note with the rationale. I'll enter it as written with that note."
      }
